---
import { site } from '../site.config';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`Why ${site.name} exists, how we approach everyday wellbeing, and what to expect from our articles.`}
>
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">A little about us</p><h1>
        Understanding makes room.
      </h1><p>
        Clear words can help us name what we are feeling. This blog is a place
        to begin.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Our purpose</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} shares educational reading about emotions, relationships, rest,
        and everyday life. We aim to explain ideas in plain English, without judgment
        or pressure to feel better on a schedule.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can explore a topic, follow a short reading path, or read one
        article and leave. There is no account to create and no right way to
        start.
      </p>
      <h2>Who writes this blog?</h2>
      <p>
        This is an early version of an independent educational project. Articles
        are currently sample drafts attributed to “Editorial team”. An
        individual author biography has not yet been supplied. We do not claim
        that these drafts have been reviewed by a clinician.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before a public launch, the site owner needs to confirm authorship, add
        an accurate biography, and arrange an editorial review. Sample labels
        will remain until that work is complete.
      </p>
      <h2>What guides our writing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Short, understandable explanations with unfamiliar terms explained.
        </li><li>
          Respect for different backgrounds, circumstances, and ways of living.
        </li><li>
          Practical ideas offered as options, without promises about outcomes.
        </li><li>
          Links to reference material and clear dates for each article.
        </li><li>Honesty about what a blog can and cannot offer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Read more in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
      <div class="callout">
        <h2>A starting point for reading</h2><p>
          This site offers general information. It does not diagnose a
          condition, provide therapy, or replace individual care. If you need
          support, our <a href="/get-help/">Get Help page</a> can help you find a
          next step.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/start-here/"
          >Find a place to start <Icon name="external" /></a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
